# Agent tooling scratch. Claude Code checks out a throwaway worktree per background
# agent here; they are transient copies of this repo, never source. Only `worktrees/`
# is ignored, so a `.claude/skills/<name>/SKILL.md` is still committable.
.claude/worktrees/

# Sibling checkouts this repository's own pipelines make *inside the workspace*, so that
# `npm run contract:check` gates rather than warns. `.chemclaw3` is
# `.github/workflows/ci.yml`'s checkout of Chemclaw3 at the pinned commit; `.jenkins-lib` is
# `Jenkinsfile`'s sparse clone. Neither is source here, and an agent or a developer who runs
# either lane locally would otherwise be offered another repository's tree to commit.
# `.chemclaw3-mock` is the `oidc-mock` job's checkout of Chemclaw3_mock, the stand-in tenant the
# real-browser sign-in runs against.
#
# Four surfaces have to agree about each of these — this file, `.dockerignore`, `.prettierignore`
# and `eslint.config.js` — and `tests/delivery.test.ts` derives the directories from the two
# pipelines rather than reading a list anybody typed here.
.chemclaw3/
.chemclaw3-mock/
.jenkins-lib/
